# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in values.
# .env.local is gitignored and must never be committed.
# NOTHING here is connected yet -- these are placeholders for later phases.

# --- Authentication (REQUIRED -- the app will not start without these) --
# This tool holds lead records, researched business profiles and draft
# outreach. Every page and every API route requires a session.
#
# Unlike every other setting in this file, these two have NO default and no
# development fallback. A built-in default for a signing secret is a published
# default: anyone reading this repository could mint a valid session. The app
# refuses to run rather than run insecurely.
#
# SESSION_SECRET signs the session cookie. At least 32 characters.
# Generate one with:  openssl rand -base64 32
# Rotating it invalidates every outstanding session, which is the only way to
# revoke one -- sessions are stateless and there is nothing server-side to
# delete.
# SESSION_SECRET=
#
# AUTH_PASSWORD is the operator's password. At least 12 characters.
# One password for one human. This is not a user database and is not trying to
# be one; the app has a single operator.
# AUTH_PASSWORD=
#
# Server-side only. NEVER prefix either with NEXT_PUBLIC_.

# --- Provider selection -------------------------------------------------
# Which implementation to load. Defaults to "mock" when unset, so a missing
# value can never cause an accidental call to a real or paid API.
# PLACES_PROVIDER=mock      # mock | osm | google
# AI_PROVIDER=mock          # mock | anthropic

# --- OpenStreetMap discovery (free, no key required) --------------------
# Real business data from OpenStreetMap via the Overpass API.
#   PLACES_PROVIDER=osm
#
# The public Overpass instance is volunteer-run community infrastructure,
# not production capacity. Keep searches deliberate; do not crawl or poll.
# Override to point at a self-hosted or paid instance.
# OVERPASS_API_URL=https://overpass-api.de/api/interpreter
#
# OSM data is © OpenStreetMap contributors, licensed ODbL 1.0. Attribution
# is rendered in the UI wherever this data is displayed.

# --- Multi-source discovery ---------------------------------------------
# Which sources one discovery run may ask, comma-separated and in order.
#
#   osm      OpenStreetMap via Overpass (free, community infrastructure)
#   google   Google Places API, Text Search (PAID -- every run is billable)
#   mock     fixtures; no network request of any kind
#
# When unset this falls back to PLACES_PROVIDER, so an existing single-provider
# configuration keeps working and means exactly what it did before. That chain
# ends at "mock", so a missing value can never cause a paid API call.
#
# A discovery run is a PREVIEW: it groups what the sources found into transient
# candidates and writes nothing. Saving OpenStreetMap results is still
# POST /api/search, which is unchanged.
# DISCOVERY_SOURCES=osm          # osm | google | mock, comma-separated

# --- Google Places (PAID -- only needed when google is a discovery source)
# Server-side only. NEVER prefix with NEXT_PUBLIC_ and never commit a real key.
# Every discovery run that includes google is one billable Text Search request;
# the field mask in the adapter decides the SKU, so it is kept minimal.
# GOOGLE_PLACES_API_KEY=

# --- Demo site generation -----------------------------------------------
# Which generator writes the sample-site copy. Defaults to "mock" when unset,
# so a missing value can never cause an accidental paid call.
#
#   mock       deterministic template copy; no network call, costs nothing
#   anthropic  Claude writes the copy. Needs ANTHROPIC_API_KEY.
#
# Separate from ANALYSIS_PROVIDER on purpose: they are two different paid
# requests, and enabling one should not silently enable the other.
#
# The model returns wording, structure and a theme ONLY. There is no field in
# its output for a name, phone, address, opening time, price or URL -- every
# fact a demo displays is supplied by application code from the lead and its
# researched profile. The prompt asks the model not to invent; the schema means
# it could not persist an invention if it tried.
# DEMO_PROVIDER=mock        # mock | anthropic

# --- Business analysis --------------------------------------------------
# Which analyser produces website strategies. Defaults to "mock" when unset,
# so a missing value can never cause an accidental paid API call.
# ANALYSIS_PROVIDER=mock    # mock | anthropic

# --- Anthropic (only needed when ANALYSIS_PROVIDER=anthropic, PAID) -----
# Server-side only. NEVER prefix with NEXT_PUBLIC_ and never commit a real
# key. Get one at https://console.anthropic.com/settings/keys
# Each analysis is one Claude request; there is no batching or retry.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# --- Business research --------------------------------------------------
# Which researcher gathers evidence for a BusinessProfile.
#
#   mock     (default) consults nothing and makes no network request
#   website  fetches the business's own homepage, when the lead lists one
#
# Website mode needs NO credential -- it reads public pages and sends none.
# It is off by default because a run reaches a third party's server on behalf
# of a business that never asked us to, so it must be a deliberate choice.
# One button click is still one lead and one bounded run; there is no bulk mode.
# RESEARCH_PROVIDER=mock    # mock | website

# --- Website lookup (PAID when set to google) ---------------------------
# When a lead's discovery record lists no website, how should research find
# one? Defaults to "off" -- nothing is looked up and no request is made.
#
#   off      (default) never look; a missing website stays "none found"
#   google   ask Google Places where this business's website is
#
# Deliberately separate from RESEARCH_PROVIDER and DISCOVERY_SOURCES: this is a
# billable per-lead request and must not switch on as a side effect.
#
# THE BOUNDARY. Google Maps Platform terms let us store a place_id indefinitely
# and lat/lng for 30 days; name, address, phone, website, rating and hours must
# be requested live and NOT warehoused. So the lookup returns ONE thing -- the
# URL -- and everything we store is our own reading of the business's own page,
# attributed to that page. Google is how we find the door, not what we record.
# WEBSITE_LOOKUP=off        # off | google

# --- Lead storage -------------------------------------------------------
# Which lead store to use. Defaults to "json" when unset, so a missing value
# can never cause an accidental connection to a real database.
# LEAD_REPOSITORY=json      # json | supabase

# --- Supabase (only needed when LEAD_REPOSITORY=supabase) ---------------
# Server-side only. The secret key bypasses Row Level Security, so it must
# NEVER be prefixed with NEXT_PUBLIC_ and never reach browser code.
# SUPABASE_URL=
# SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=
#
# Apply supabase/migrations/ before selecting the supabase repository.
# The migration enables RLS with no policies: all access is server-side.
